{"track":"odes","num":"3.01","title":"Second-Order Linear Homogeneous Equations","sub":null,"sections":[{"heading":"The auxiliary equation","questions":[{"q":"Write the auxiliary (characteristic) equation for $y'' - 5y' + 6y = 0$.","answer":"$r^2 - 5r + 6 = 0$."},{"q":"Write and simplify the auxiliary equation for $2y'' + 4y' - 6y = 0$.","answer":"$2r^2 + 4r - 6 = 0$, which simplifies to $r^2 + 2r - 3 = 0$."}]},{"heading":"Distinct real roots","questions":[{"q":"Solve $y'' - 5y' + 6y = 0$.","answer":"$r^2-5r+6=(r-2)(r-3)=0 \\Rightarrow r = 2, 3$. General solution: $y = C_1e^{2x} + C_2e^{3x}$."},{"q":"Solve $y'' + 2y' - 3y = 0$, $y(0)=1$, $y'(0)=1$.","answer":"$r^2+2r-3=(r+3)(r-1)=0 \\Rightarrow r=-3,1$. So $y=C_1e^{-3x}+C_2e^{x}$. From $y(0)=1$: $C_1+C_2=1$. From $y'(0)=1$: $-3C_1+C_2=1$. Subtracting gives $4C_1=0$, so $C_1=0$, $C_2=1$. Thus $y = e^{x}$."}]},{"heading":"Repeated roots","questions":[{"q":"Solve $y'' - 6y' + 9y = 0$.","answer":"$r^2-6r+9=(r-3)^2=0 \\Rightarrow r=3$ (repeated). General solution: $y = (C_1+C_2x)e^{3x}$."},{"q":"Solve $y'' + 4y' + 4y = 0$, $y(0)=2$, $y'(0)=-1$.","answer":"$r^2+4r+4=(r+2)^2=0 \\Rightarrow r=-2$. So $y=(C_1+C_2x)e^{-2x}$. From $y(0)=2$: $C_1=2$. Differentiating, $y' = C_2e^{-2x} - 2(C_1+C_2x)e^{-2x}$; $y'(0) = C_2 - 2C_1 = -1 \\Rightarrow C_2 = 2(2)-1=3$. Thus $y=(2+3x)e^{-2x}$."}]},{"heading":"Complex roots","questions":[{"q":"Solve $y'' + 4y = 0$.","answer":"$r^2+4=0 \\Rightarrow r=\\pm 2i$. General solution: $y = C_1\\cos 2x + C_2\\sin 2x$."},{"q":"Solve $y'' - 2y' + 5y = 0$.","answer":"$r^2-2r+5=0 \\Rightarrow r=\\dfrac{2\\pm\\sqrt{4-20}}{2}=1\\pm 2i$. General solution: $y = e^{x}(C_1\\cos 2x + C_2\\sin 2x)$."}]},{"heading":"Application: a damped spring","questions":[{"q":"A mass–spring–damper system satisfies $y'' + 4y' + 5y = 0$. Find the general solution and classify the damping (over/critically/under-damped).","answer":"$r^2+4r+5=0$, discriminant $=16-20=-4<0$, so $r=-2\\pm i$. General solution: $y = e^{-2x}(C_1\\cos x + C_2\\sin x)$ — this is under-damped (complex roots with negative real part give oscillatory decay)."},{"q":"Solve $y'' + 6y' + 9y = 0$, $y(0)=1$, $y'(0)=0$, and classify the damping.","answer":"$r^2+6r+9=(r+3)^2=0 \\Rightarrow r=-3$ (repeated) — critically damped. So $y=(C_1+C_2x)e^{-3x}$. From $y(0)=1$: $C_1=1$. $y'=C_2e^{-3x}-3(C_1+C_2x)e^{-3x}$; $y'(0)=C_2-3C_1=0 \\Rightarrow C_2=3$. Thus $y=(1+3x)e^{-3x}$."}]}]}